  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1210 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nLong story short, hot temperatures remain in the forecast with the \nmajority of the Panhandles reaching the 100-109 degree range in the \nafternoon with very little cooling at night. After Sunday, the \neastern Panhandles may lose the 60 Tds leading to a bit of a drier \nheat as apposed to the high heat indices that have been seen lately. \nDry air may be able to mix down especially Tue and Wed allowing \nmuch drier conditions for the central to southwestern TX \nPanhandle, which could very well lead to elevated fire weather \nconditions as drought persists. Through the long term very little\nchance of precip exist except for the northwest come Thu when the\nhigh may shift and bring northwest flow and some slight chance to\nchance PoPs to the northwestern corner of the combined \nPanhandles.",
